    description: "WHAT (as reported)\nExpress (the express repository's examples/): 7 of about 54 app.get / app.post / ... calls were reported as routes, without handler names, and a route \"ALL /\" was reported at line 1 of lib/application.js that the code does not declare.\n\nNOT CHECKED\nWhich call shapes the 47 misses have (router objects, chained .route(), handlers passed as arrays). The unreleased changelog adds Express middleware entry points; whether it changes route counts is not known.\n\nREPORTED, NOT RE-RUN. Source: an outside reviewer who tried hypergumbo 10.0.0 from PyPI on 2026-11-24 (transcript pasted by the owner in session). Nothing in this item was run on dev by the filing agent unless a line says so; the reviewer's fixtures are not on this machine. FIRST STEP: reproduce on current dev with a fixture, and check the unreleased changelog, before building anything. Filed at the owner's request (\"file them all now\")."  # b931
